instructions:
You are working in the JavaScript repository /luxon (the luxon date library, tests via jest). Your job is a single, precise bug fix in /luxon/src/interval.js, then verification. Do not change any other file, and do not modify any existing test file.

THE BUG: `Interval.fromISO(text, opts)` currently calls `DateTime.fromISO(s, opts)` and `DateTime.fromISO(e, opts)` directly. When `Settings.throwOnInvalid === true`, `DateTime.fromISO` THROWS on unparseable input, so a perfectly valid duration-based interval such as `Interval.fromISO("2016-01-01/P1Y")` or `Interval.fromISO("P1Y/2016-01-01")` throws instead of returning the interval. It should instead fall through to the duration-parsing branches and return the valid Interval (and only throw for genuinely unparsable input, via `Interval.invalid(...)`).

THE FIX: replace the body of `static fromISO(text, opts)` in /luxon/src/interval.js (currently lines ~134-157) with exactly this:

```js
  static fromISO(text, opts) {
    const [s, e] = (text || "").split("/", 2);
    if (s && e) {
      let start, startIsValid;
      try {
        start = DateTime.fromISO(s, opts);
        startIsValid = start.isValid;
      } catch (e) {
        startIsValid = false;
      }

      let end, endIsValid;
      try {
        end = DateTime.fromISO(e, opts);
        endIsValid = end.isValid;
      } catch (e) {
        endIsValid = false;
      }

      if (startIsValid && endIsValid) {
        return Interval.fromDateTimes(start, end);
      }

      if (startIsValid) {
        const dur = Duration.fromISO(e, opts);
        if (dur.isValid) {
          return Interval.after(start, dur);
        }
      } else if (endIsValid) {
        const dur = Duration.fromISO(s, opts);
        if (dur.isValid) {
          return Interval.before(end, dur);
        }
      }
    }
    return Interval.invalid("unparsable", `the input "${text}" can't be parsed asISO 8601`);
  }
```

Keep the surrounding JSDoc comment untouched. Keep code style (prettier, 2-space indent, double quotes).

VERIFICATION (do all of it, and report the raw output):
1. Write a temporary verification script OUTSIDE the repo test tree, e.g. /tmp/iso_check.js, that imports from "/luxon/src/luxon.js" (use `import { Interval, Settings } from "/luxon/src/luxon.js";` with ES module syntax) and asserts, with `Settings.throwOnInvalid = true`:
   - `Interval.fromISO("2016-01-01/2016-12-31")` does not throw, is valid, start zoneName is the default zone;
   - `Interval.fromISO("2016-01-01/P1Y")` does not throw and is valid;
   - `Interval.fromISO("P1Y/2016-01-01")` does not throw and is valid;
   - `Interval.fromISO("2016-01-01/P1Y", { zone: "Europe/Paris" })` does not throw, is valid, and `start.zoneName === "Europe/Paris"`;
   - `Interval.fromISO("hello")` DOES throw (unparsable);
   - `Interval.fromISO("foo/bar")` DOES throw;
   - then with `Settings.throwOnInvalid = false`: `Interval.fromISO("hello").isValid === false` and `invalidReason === "unparsable"`; `Interval.fromISO("2016-01-01/P1Y").isValid === true`.
   Run it with: `cd /luxon && npx babel-node /tmp/iso_check.js` (babel-node is a devDependency). If babel-node cannot run a file outside the repo, instead put the script at /luxon/tmp_iso_check.js, run it, and DELETE it afterwards. Report the exact command and its full output.
2. Run the existing interval tests: `cd /luxon && npx jest test/interval 2>&1 | tail -n 40`. Report pass/fail counts and any failures.
3. Run the full suite: `cd /luxon && npx jest 2>&1 | tail -n 40`. Report pass/fail counts and the names of any failing tests (there may be pre-existing failures unrelated to this change; list them all).
4. Confirm `git -C /luxon status --porcelain` shows ONLY src/interval.js as modified (plus untracked temp files you must delete). Delete any temp files you created.

Report: the exact diff of src/interval.js (`git -C /luxon diff src/interval.js`), the verification outputs, and any remaining failures with their names.

