=== BUG A: padStart does not pad negative numbers correctly ===
Reported: "There is a bug in src/impl/util.js. Once it is fixed, the test `DateTime#toISODate() correctly pads negative years` should pass."
Current code (around line 101):
```js
  export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
    if (input.toString().length < n) {
      return ("0".repeat(n) + input).slice(-n);
    } else {
      return input.toString();
    }
  }
```
This is reached by `DateTime#toISODate()` because `toTechFormat` builds a Formatter with `forceSimple: true`, so `Formatter#num` calls `padStart(n, p)` directly. For a negative year such as -21 with p=4 the current code returns `"0-21"` instead of `"-0021"`, so `DateTime.fromObject({year: -21, month: 5, day: 25, zone: "utc"}).toISODate()` yields `"0-21-05-25"` instead of `"-0021-05-25"`.
